What I found:
• #1062 is still broken, checked tonight. I pointed the binary at a local server that always returns 401 and passed the key with --api-key. The error hint still said OPENAI_API_KEY is not set and told me to "use --api-key", which I had just done. The cause is in src/prompt_retry.rs:527: it checks only one environment variable, so it can't see a key given on the command line or in config. The other half of #1062 is the setup wizard opening even when --api-key was given; that check is in setup::needs_setup_from, called from src/main.rs:1033. I read that code but didn't rerun it in a terminal tonight. Nothing has been committed against #1062 since it was filed.
• #1064 is no longer on hold. My journal still calls it "held", but the latest comment on the issue corrects that: @yuanhao handed the decision back on 10-21. The new question is whether model-driven subprocesses get the API key stripped by default:
  • Today only the model's bash gets the key stripped, and only with the opt-in.
  • Hooks are easy to change: yoyo starts them itself (src/hooks.rs:741).
  • MCP servers are the hard part. yoagent 0.25.12 starts them in mcp/transport.rs:117-129 and only lets yoyo add environment variables, not remove them. The ways around that are wrapping the server command in env -u (Unix only) or filing an upstream request.
• #1063 (`/bg` and `/watch` waiting forever on a backgrounded child) and #1057 (the stale-worktree sweep can delete a live worker's worktree) both come from reading the code; I haven't reproduced either.
• Research: the Claude Code releases from Oct 20–22 mostly change what the model is told: refused tool calls, compaction dropping old messages, a subagent switching to a fallback model. They also stop errors being sent down the wrong recovery path. yoyo has no special message for a full disk (no ENOSPC anywhere in src). I didn't check whether the model is told when compaction drops messages. I saved one note on this to yopedia.

Suggested order for the planner: #1062 first, then the next #1064 decision, then #1063.

