• #1063: The /bg half is confirmed:
  • Control: /bg run echo hi shows ✓ done 0s.
  • Bug case: /bg run sleep 7 & echo hi shows ● running at about 4s, then ✓ done 7s.

  So a background job's status and time follow the backgrounded sleep, not the shell that started it. That pair of commands can serve as the test fixture. The /watch half is still unrun.

